I pulled Cloudflare's live job board (Greenhouse API), filtered to engineering roles whose descriptions mention Rust, and looked up each role's real office locations. Here are 5:

```json
[
  {
    "title": "Principal Software Engineer, Workers Deploy & Config",
    "location": "Austin, TX (In-Office)",
    "link": "https://boards.greenhouse.io/cloudflare/jobs/8055320"
  },
  {
    "title": "Senior Distributed Systems Engineer",
    "location": "Austin, TX (In-Office)",
    "link": "https://boards.greenhouse.io/cloudflare/jobs/8066716"
  },
  {
    "title": "Senior Distributed Systems Engineer - Cache",
    "location": "Hybrid: Atlanta, Austin, Champaign, New York, San Francisco, Seattle, Washington DC",
    "link": "https://boards.greenhouse.io/cloudflare/jobs/8163523"
  },
  {
    "title": "Engineering Manager, Cloudflare Network Interconnect",
    "location": "Austin, TX (Hybrid)",
    "link": "https://boards.greenhouse.io/cloudflare/jobs/8083701"
  },
  {
    "title": "Engineering Manager - Workers Runtime, Edge Team",
    "location": "Austin, TX; Lisbon; London; Seattle (In-Office)",
    "link": "https://boards.greenhouse.io/cloudflare/jobs/7653558"
  }
]
```

- **Match method:** The filter was a word match for "Rust" in the posting text, and I didn't read each posting in full. About 62 of the 435 open postings mention it, so there are more to choose from.
- **Location data:** The board's main location field only says "Hybrid" or "In-Office". The cities above come from each role's office list.
- **Links:** They go to the Greenhouse board that powers cloudflare.com/careers/jobs.

